@startuml payment-business-process
!include <archimate/Archimate>
title Online Payment Processing - Business Process
caption Viewpoint: ArchiMate Business Process | Layer: Business | To-Be | R=BA A=Owner C=SA,Sec,Test I=Dev,Ops | Status Draft
top to bottom direction
Business_Actor(merchant, "Merchant")
Business_Process(receive, "Receive payment operation")
Business_Process(validate, "Validate request and idempotency")
Business_Process(fraud, "Authorization fraud gate")
Business_Process(route, "Route operation to Acquirer")
Business_Process(record, "Record Payment lifecycle state")
Business_Process(publish, "Publish status-change event")
Business_Process(deliver, "Deliver signed webhook")
Business_Process(query, "Serve payment query from gateway data")
Business_Object(payment, "Payment")
Rel_Assignment(merchant, receive, "initiates")
Rel_Triggering(receive, validate, "triggers")
Rel_Triggering(validate, fraud, "CON.2: authorization only")
Rel_Triggering(fraud, route, "pass")
Rel_Triggering(fraud, record, "block -> Declined")
Rel_Triggering(route, record, "approved / declined / failed")
Rel_Triggering(record, publish, "CON.4: async")
Rel_Triggering(publish, deliver, "async queue")
Rel_Access(record, payment, "writes")
Rel_Access(query, payment, "reads gateway data")
legend bottom
ArchiMate only. G2 evidence: Payment lifecycle states and CON.2/CON.4 decision branches.
endlegend
@enduml